  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Cherry has a matrix AAA consisting of NNN rows and MMM columns, filled with lowercase English letters.\n\nYou are asked QQQ queries. Each query is provided by four integers x1x_{1}x1​, y1y_{1}y1​, x2x_{2}x2​, y2y_{2}y2​ which define the rectangle, where (x1x_{1}x1​, y1y_{1}y1​) stands for the coordinates of the top left cell of the rectangle, while (x2x_{2}x2​, y2y_{2}y2​) stands for the coordinates of the bottom right cell. The answer to the query is the size of the maximum square, that is located fully inside the query rectangle such that :\n\n\nThe characters of each row should be in non-decreasing order.\nThe characters of each column should be in non-decreasing order.\nNote: x1x_{1}x1​ represents the row number while y1y_{1}y1​ represents the column number.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nThe first line of the input contains two integers NNN and MMM — the number of rows and the number of columns in the matrix.\nEach of the next NNN lines contains a string of MMM lowercase English letters denoting one row of the matrix.\nNext line contains an integer QQQ — the number of queries.\nThen follow QQQ lines with queries descriptions. Each of them contains four integers x1x_{1}x1​, y1y_{1}y1​, x2x_{2}x2​, y2y_{2}y2​ — coordinates of the up left and bottom right cells of the query rectangle.\n###Output:\n\nPrint QQQ  lines. The iii-th of them should contain the maximum size of the square for the iii-th query.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤N,M≤5001 \\leq N,M \\leq 5001≤N,M≤500\n1≤Q≤1051 \\leq Q \\leq 10^51≤Q≤105\n1≤x1≤x2≤N1 \\leq x_{1} \\leq x_{2} \\leq N1≤x1​≤x2​≤N\n1≤y1≤y2≤M1 \\leq y_{1} \\leq y_{2} \\leq M1≤y1​≤y2​≤M\n###Sample Input:\n\n`4 4\r\naaaa\r\nbbaa\r\ncdef\r\nwxyz\r\n3\r\n1 1 4 4\r\n1 2 2 3\r\n3 1 4 4\n`###Sample Output:\n\n`2\r\n1\r\n2\n`###Explanation:\n\n**Example Case 1:**\n\n**Query 1:** The maximum size square that lies inside the query rectangle is **2**. One of the such squares is:\n\n[aabb]\\begin{bmatrix} aa \\\\ bb \\end{bmatrix}[aabb​]\n\n**Query 2:** The maximum size square that lies inside the query rectangle is **1**. One of the such square is:\n\n[a]\\begin{bmatrix} a \\end{bmatrix}[a​]\n\n**Query 3:** The maximum size square that lies inside the query rectangle is **2**. One of the such square is:\n\n[dexy]\\begin{bmatrix} de \\\\ xy \\end{bmatrix}[dexy​]",
